  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer is the strongest combination (0.725 weighted, 0.721 concat), and transformer aggregation clearly outperforms avgpool. However, config_015 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) showed the highest F1 (0.6945) of all experiments despite lower accuracy, suggesting resnet50 captures complementary class-discriminative features. Question: Does the untested resnet50 + concat fusion interaction (config_023) yield a configuration that could rival or exceed 0.725? This completes the 2x2 (image_encoder × fusion) grid under the best RNA encoder and aggregation, reducing uncertainty about whether a different image-fusion pairing could outperform our current best. Why this is the best use of experiment 7: With only 3 experiments remaining, testing the closest untested neighbor to our best result is the highest-information, lowest-risk choice. If it performs near 0.725, it confirms config_001 as optimal; if it exceeds it, we gain a new best. Either outcome sharpens our final 3 experiments toward exploitation of the confirmed best configuration."
